{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794737462,"nonce":"LwAPsH0nFZZTXwEpAzRdN+9C1I8=","message":"P0 audit, part 2: what genhl does, against what AIR has and what the file carries (genhl.ml, hlcode.ml, Haxe 4.3.6; two read passes, spot-checked against the source).\n\nVerdict: nAIR lowering is a port of genhl's evaluation layer that emits AIR, plus a whole-program pre-pass. AIR has an Instr or Terminator for every HL operation the audit found (Call, CallMethod, CallClosure, Static/Instance/VirtualClosure, Get/SetGlobal, Field and Dyn get/set, Cast with ToDyn/ToSFloat/ToUFloat/ToInt/SafeCast/UnsafeCast/ToVirtual, NullCheck, New, EnumAlloc/MakeEnum/EnumField/SetEnumField/EnumIndex, Cell* and Ref ops, Switch, Trap, EndTrap, Throw, Rethrow). No new instruction is needed for P1 or P2.\n\nWhole-program pre-pass (cannot be per function):\n- `overrides`: a method gets a virtual slot only if some class in the program overrides it; every call site depends on it. Slot order is declaration order, an override reuses the parent's slot, and ArrayAccess getDyn/setDyn must be slots 0 and 1.\n- Type tables: cached types, anonymous-structure types (HVirtual, fields sorted by name), interface types (own fields in descending name order, then extended interfaces reversed), closure environments (tuple enums). Two structurally equal anonymous types or interfaces collapse into one runtime type.\n- Pools and ids: strings, ints, floats, bytes, globals ($Class, enum constructors, string constants), natives (alloc_array, alloc_bytes, dyn_op, itos, ftos, string_compare), function ids, method wrappers.\n- Start-up function: Type.init guard, registration of every class, enum and core type (with __meta__), every cl_init, every static variable initializer, then main, each in com.types order.\n- The runtime computes byte offsets, hash tables, mark bits and method tables from the serialized descriptors on first use. Reordering fields or leaving gaps in fvirtual ids breaks the ABI.\n\nSemantics a lowering must keep (each is a place a clean SSA lowering would differ):\n- Unchecked `cast e` is a runtime-checked SafeCast. Casts between Bool and number, `Null\u003cInt\u003e` to another int kind, and anything to `Null\u003cInt64\u003e` abort at compile time.\n- `unsigned_op` counts every Int literal as unsigned. Mod and shift read unsignedness from the left operand; `/` is always signed; UInt to float is signed except in an explicit cast.\n- `Dynamic` against a number compares as Float, so `(null:Dynamic) == 0` is true.\n- Evaluation order: `new` allocates before its arguments; a call evaluates and null-checks the receiver before the arguments; a static-variable assignment evaluates the value before loading the global; a Dynamic field assignment does not coerce the value.\n- Prefix `++x` returns the variable's own register, while reads of a local copy it.\n- Array reads past the end return the default; writes past the end call __expand; only a negative index throws. Array field 0 is length, field 1 the data. String is bytes then length.\n- Dense switch: every case a constant Int in 0..255. A `Null\u003cInt\u003e` subject becomes 0 and matches `case 0`. Otherwise the subject is evaluated once and tests run before bodies; string switches compare UTF-16 length, then string_compare.\n- try/catch: `hl.BaseType.check` per typed catch in source order, a Dynamic catch ends the chain, fall-through rethrows. EndTrap is emitted once per active trap before return, break and continue. Exceptions are the thrown Dynamic, unwrapped.\n- Do-while `continue` jumps to the body start. It is correct only because the analyzer rewrites it to `if(!cond) break; continue`, so a field with `@:analyzer(ignore)` would break it.\n- Optional parameters with a default, and optional parameters whose type is not nullable, are HRef at the ABI: callers pass a pointer to a held copy or a null ref, and the callee materializes the default.\n- Closures: captured variables are copied into the environment at creation (a captured and reassigned variable was already wrapped into a 1-element array by the CPWrapRef filter). One captured nullable variable is the environment itself; none gives a static closure; a child whose captures are all in the parent reuses the parent's environment.\n- Runtime helpers called by name must stay alive: String.__add__, __alloc__, call_toString; Std.__add__, string; hl.BaseType.check; ArrayDyn.get_length, alloc; ArrayObj.alloc; ArrayBase.alloc{I32,UI16,F32,F64}; each array class's __expand; Reflect._makeVarArgs; Type.init, initClass, initEnum, register; and the pproto hooks __string, __compare, __cast, __get_field.\n\nWhat the file needs and lacks (all are exporter work; the unit suite is the oracle):\n1. cl_init per class, and com.types order (the writers sort it away).\n2. Metadata: @:hlNative (class and field, with arguments), @:struct, @:packed, @:coreType, @:realPath, @:noExpr, and the runtime @:meta that Texpr.build_metadata reads.\n3. Field kind: physical or not (non-physical vars take no layout slot), MethDynamic, extern. Only static/method/final/inline/public/override are flagged today.\n4. The optional bit on function-type arguments. The writers drop it (`(_, _, t)`), and to_type needs it for HRef.\n5. To verify: type-parameter constraints (to_type uses the first non-interface constraint), com.resources for `$resources`, the hl-ver define for the @:hlNative version gate (compared as strings), the -debug flag (adds checks after unsafe casts).\n\nNot audited: Hlopt (the bytecode optimizer, semantics preserving), HLC and hl2c, and the debug-info writer.\n\nOrder of work: (a) the file additions above, measured against the unit suite; (b) a Rust crate that builds the whole-program context from the file, checked by comparing its type, slot and global tables with the ones genhl writes into a .hl; (c) the P1 subset lowering, checked against hello, fib, nbody and the BM kernels run through the .hl path.","files":null}]}